invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_field.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: zero_mask_word takes its mask from the borrow of 0 - v. The mask
  is the same, so every vector, proof and count under clang passes. On
  the overflow builtins, gcc 13.3 and 15.2 for x86-64 compiled that
  borrow to a jump on v at -O2, and v is the words of a coordinate: the
  Z of a product in p256_wide_point_affine, and the Y p256_wide_fe_neg
  negates. gcc reads another form of the step by default, and a build
  that names the builtins reads this one. No check of this tree counts
  these files' branches under a 64-bit gcc, so the Semgrep rule
  inv-16-p256-wide-no-borrow-from-zero refuses the call.

--- old
    uint64_t nonzero = (uint64_t)(((ct_u128)v + UINT64_MAX) >> 64);
    return p256_wide_mask(nonzero ^ 1U);
--- new
    uint64_t borrow = 0;
    (void)p256_wide_sub_borrow(&borrow, 0, v);
    return ~p256_wide_mask(borrow);
